# Annigems — Architecture

## Layered structure

```
Controller      -> HTTP only: receive request, call service, return response/view
Form Request    -> all validation; never inline in controller
Service Class   -> all business logic
Repository      -> non-trivial database queries
Model           -> relationships, scopes, casts, accessors only
Helper          -> small reusable pure functions
Resource        -> API response shaping (where APIs exist)
Enum            -> fixed value sets (statuses, roles, purities, payment methods)
Event/Listener  -> side effects (audit logging, stock movement recording)
```

## Mandatory rules

- Controllers stay thin (~15 lines max per method). Longer logic belongs in a service.
- Every module gets its own Service (e.g. `BranchService`, `JewelleryItemService`).
- Never raw validation in controllers — always Form Request classes.
- Never hardcode status/role strings — use PHP Enums (e.g. `ItemStatus::AVAILABLE`, `UserRole::CASHIER`).
- Multi-table writes must use database transactions; roll back on any failure.
- Authorize with Policies/Gates — never scattered `if ($user->role == 'admin')`.
- Use Route Model Binding where appropriate.
- Group routes by role/middleware; split into `routes/superadmin.php`, `routes/admin.php`, etc. when large.
- All schema changes via migrations; seeders for SuperAdmin, roles, permissions, categories, purities.
- Follow PSR-12.

## Naming

| Kind | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Controller | Singular + Controller | `BranchController` |
| Service | Singular + Service | `BranchService` |
| Form Request | Store/Update + Model | `StoreBranchRequest` |
| Model | Singular | `JewelleryItem` |
| Table | plural snake_case | `jewellery_items` |
| Blade | module folders | `resources/views/superadmin/branches/index.blade.php` |
| Enum | `App\Enums\*` | `UserRole`, `ItemStatus` |

## Cross-cutting quality

- **No duplicate code** — extract to service, helper, trait, or Blade component.
- **AJAX JSON shape:** `{ success: bool, message: string, data: mixed, errors: object }`.
- **Audit logging** on create/update/delete of important records (items, invoices, users, branches, settings): who, what changed, when.
- **Soft deletes** on items, invoices, customers, users (and similar never-truly-lost records).
- **Timezone and currency** defined once in config — never hardcoded in views.
- **Secrets** only via `.env` — nothing sensitive hardcoded.
